==== hyperbricks yaml {!{greeting}} ====
greeting:
  - type: goja_render
  - script: |
      function main(input) {
        return { message: input.values.message };
      }
  - values:
      message: Hello from the server
  - inline: '<p>{{.Data.message}}</p>'
==== explainer ====
Run trusted server-side JavaScript in a fresh runtime per request. The returned object is available as .Data in the Go HTML template. Use the existing file resolver under script to load source from resources; see GOJA_RENDER.md for the file-based example and execution limits.
==== expected json ====
{
  "AllowedQueryKeys": null,
  "ConfigCategory": "",
  "ConfigType": "<GOJA_RENDER>",
  "Enclose": "",
  "ExtraAttributes": null,
  "HyperBricksFile": "",
  "HyperBricksKey": "",
  "HyperBricksPath": "",
  "Inline": "<p>{{.Data.message}}</p>",
  "MetaDocDescription": "",
  "Script": "function main(input) {\n  return { message: input.values.message };\n}\n",
  "Template": "",
  "Timeout": "",
  "Values": { "message": "Hello from the server" }
}
==== expected output ====
<p>Hello from the server</p>
